From c031d529f4799ab45bf112cb952eff960306957e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:04:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the waiting screen in the game's look, from the
 player's game files

srnp_game_textures: the runner reads pictures from the player's game
(<game root>/files), never from this repository: the game's LZSS is
undone, the N-th GVR texture found, its CI4/CI8 texels decoded with
their RGB5A3 palette and made into a texture of the video backend for
ImGui (cached; on the video thread). The labels mod's own texture
("5P".."8P" after the SRNPLBL1 block of its GTSE) is read from the mod
folders when the mod is there.

The waiting screen now uses them (Gibax's choices): the menus' blue,
the game's "ARE YOU READY?" (menus, picture 38), one card a seat on the
menus' panel (116) tinted, the game's labels (1P..4P and COM from the
HUD atlas, as the game's table at 0x805D3DB4 has them; 5P..8P from the
labels mod, drawn without it), the characters' heads from the HUD atlas
(entries 5 + character of the same table), the menus' "?" for a seat
the AI takes over. The counts keep ImGui's font: the game has no
complete alphabet (pre-drawn words, and text fonts holding only their
messages' glyphs).

Measured: 6 seats, one leaves, photographed in the real window; the
race behind it 28 checksums equal, 0 divergences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
